verview","desc":"For a Ph.D. minor, the department requires 20 units of Classics coursework at the graduate level (i.e. courses numbered 200 and above). Other courses can count towards this requirement with written consent from the Director of Graduate Studies and notification to the Student Services Manager.\nThose pursuing a Ph.D. minor in Classics must take one course in the Latin Core or Greek Core sequence. The remaining units (typically graduate seminars) must be selected in consultation with the candidate’s Classics advisor or Director of Graduate Studies. Before obtaining Classics department approval, students interested in this minor must discuss their proposed course plan with the Director of Graduate Studies and their Ph.D. department.","t":"text","info":true}],"kind":"info"}]}